<Layouts.marketing flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope} page_title={@page_title}>
  <%!-- ───────────── HERO ─────────────
        Sibling of /design-system. That page opens in the vocabulary of "my site
        looks like everyone else's"; this one opens in the vocabulary people
        actually use for the other half — "it keeps breaking" and "it changed
        something I didn't ask it to". Nobody says "unreliable". --%>
  <section class="bg-base-200 border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="badge badge-primary badge-outline gap-2 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
          Plain English · no tests to write · no code to read
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.05]">
          Decide what it does <span class="text-primary">once.</span>
        </h1>
      </div>

      <%!-- Same treatment as /design-system's hero: self-hosted rather than a
           YouTube embed, poster plus native controls, preload="none" so the page
           pays only for the poster until someone presses play. --%>
      <figure class="mt-10">
        <div class="rounded-box overflow-hidden border border-base-300 shadow-sm bg-base-300">
          <video
            id="behavior-hero-video"
            class="w-full aspect-video block"
            controls
            playsinline
            preload="none"
            width="1920"
            height="1080"
            poster="https://images.codemyspec.com/behavior-hero-poster.jpg"
          >
            <source src="https://images.codemyspec.com/behavior-hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            Your browser cannot play this video.
          </video>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="text-sm text-base-content/60 mt-3">
          One story, from a sentence you wrote to a check that keeps it true. 2 min.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mt-10">
        <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-base-content">
            Describe what your software should do, in your own words. Agree the rules in a
            conversation. Everything built after that has to keep those rules true.
          </strong>
          You never write a test and you never read the code.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <.link navigate={~p"/install"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Install the plugin — free</.link>
          <.link navigate={~p"/design-system"} class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">
            The other half: how it looks →
          </.link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── THE PROBLEM ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.eyebrow name="why it keeps breaking" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        Nobody wrote down what it was supposed to do.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-lg text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-base-content">
            You described a feature once, in a chat, and then it scrolled away.
          </strong>
          Nothing kept a record of what you asked for. So when you add the next feature, nothing
          is checking that the last one still works — and the first time you find out it doesn't
          is when a customer tells you.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is the same failure as a project that looks like every other project, pointed at a
          different target. There, nobody decided how it should look, so the model used the average.
          Here, nobody decided what it should do, so every change is a guess about what you meant
          three weeks ago.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-sm text-base-content/60 leading-relaxed">
        The longer version, with what actually goes wrong in production, is in
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/blog/ai-app-breaks-in-production"}
          class="link link-hover text-base-content/80"
        >
          why AI-built apps break in production
        </.link>
        .
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── HOW IT WORKS ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.eyebrow name="how it works" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        A conversation, then rules that outlive it.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-base-content">
          You write one sentence about what you want. Everything after that comes out of talking it
          through.
        </strong>
        No document to maintain, and nothing to keep in sync by hand.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mt-12">
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 border-t-4 border-t-primary shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-primary">
              You say it
            </span>
            <h3 class="card-title mt-1">One sentence, your words.</h3>
            <p class="text-base-content/70">
              "I want to group my work into projects and release them when I'm ready." That is the
              whole input. No diagrams, no tickets, nothing technical.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 border-t-4 border-t-secondary shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-secondary">
              You talk it through
            </span>
            <h3 class="card-title mt-1">The rules fall out.</h3>
            <p class="text-base-content/70">
              The conversation turns that sentence into the rules that actually govern it, and an
              example of each — including the ones where things go wrong. Questions nobody can
              answer get raised, not guessed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 border-t-4 border-t-accent shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-accent">
              It holds
            </span>
            <h3 class="card-title mt-1">Every rule becomes a check.</h3>
            <p class="text-base-content/70">
              Each example turns into something that runs. Change anything, and every rule you ever
              agreed to is checked again before the change is allowed to stand.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── TWO CHECKS ─────────────
        The distinction the video is built around, and the thing most people
        have not seen: constant checking is a different job from the final
        walkthrough, and conflating them loses both. --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.eyebrow name="two checks, two jobs" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        A supervisor on site, and an inspector at the end.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        If you were putting up a building you would not choose between the two, and you would not
        confuse them either.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-12">
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-primary">
              Every single change
            </span>
            <h3 class="card-title mt-1">The supervisor.</h3>
            <p class="text-base-content/70">
              Every rule you agreed to runs again, on every change, holding the work up against
              what was decided. Something stops being true and you hear about it that hour, not
              that quarter.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-secondary">
              Once, at the end
            </span>
            <h3 class="card-title mt-1">The inspector.</h3>
            <p class="text-base-content/70">
              Before a piece of work is called done, an agent opens the application and uses it the
              way you would — clicking through the real thing, not reading the code that built it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── HONEST LIMITS ─────────────
        Mirrors /design-system's section of the same name. Naming the limits is
        what makes the rest credible, and this audience has been oversold to. --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.eyebrow name="what it does not do" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        It cannot decide whether the idea was right.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-lg text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          It will hold your software to what you said. It will not tell you that what you said was
          a bad idea, that customers wanted something else, or that the feature was not worth
          building. Deciding whether it is good enough stays yours.
        </p>
        <p>
          It also cannot check a rule nobody agreed to. If a case never comes up in the
          conversation, nothing is watching it — which is the honest reason the conversation is
          worth an afternoon.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── HOW IT FITS ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.eyebrow name="how it fits" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        The other half of the same decision.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-lg text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Two questions get asked about AI-built software more than any others. Why does it look
          like everything else, and why does it keep breaking. They have the same answer: nobody
          decided, so the machine decided.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <.link navigate={~p"/design-system"} class="btn btn-outline">
          Decide how it looks once →
        </.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/product"} class="btn btn-ghost">See the whole process →</.link>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── FAQ ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.eyebrow name="questions" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
        Questions we get.
      </h2>
      <.faq faqs={@faqs} name="behavior-faq" class="max-w-3xl" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── CTA ───────────── --%>
  <section class="bg-base-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        Decide what it does once.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mt-4 max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Free to build with. Bring the software you already started.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <.link navigate={~p"/install"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Install the plugin — free</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/vibe-coding-rebuild"} class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">
          Or have it rebuilt for you →
        </.link>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.marketing>
